WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.360
At the bottom of the hill, make a right.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.775
Continue straight ahead.

00:00:11.618 --> 00:00:13.800
At the&nbsp;next intersection, turn left.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:21.960
My name is Karen Jacobson and I'm known as&nbsp;the only woman men will take directions from.

00:00:22.547 --> 00:00:30.300
My speaking voice ended up in over a billion GPS&nbsp;and smartphone devices giving directions to people&nbsp;around the world.

00:00:31.122 --> 00:00:33.901
You have reached your destination.

00:00:34.061 --> 00:00:35.778
Well I'll take you right back to the beginning...

00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:40.784
I'm originally from Mackay, which is a town in North&nbsp;Queensland near Australia's Great Barrier Reef.

00:00:41.051 --> 00:00:44.390
I wanted to become a professional singer and&nbsp;move to America.

00:00:44.497 --> 00:00:48.429
And I did follow that dream to New York.

00:00:48.568 --> 00:00:52.674
And not long after I moved there,&nbsp;there was an audition 

00:00:52.738 --> 00:00:59.816
and a client was looking&nbsp;for a native Australian female voiceover artist&nbsp;living in the northeast of the United States.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.853
And I went to that audition and I got the job.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:07.242
Proceed to&nbsp;the route. Proceed to the route. Proceed to the route.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:12.587
At the time I was told that the Australian&nbsp;
voice was a high priority 

00:01:12.832 --> 00:01:22.703
because the Australian&nbsp;accent was considered the most pleasant English-speaking accent to listen to

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:24.660
which is pretty cool.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.732
Turn left. At the roundabout, turn right.

00:01:28.403 --> 00:01:34.505
There was a huge script, a massive script, and the team of engineers had figured out

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:38.761
every combination&nbsp;of syllables possible for me to record

00:01:38.761 --> 00:01:43.153
so they could chop that up and create this voice system&nbsp;based on my speaking voice.

00:01:43.153 --> 00:01:47.610
I went into the booth and recorded these different lines.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:55.429
At the next&nbsp;intersection, turn left. At the roundabout, turn right. You have reached your destination.

00:01:55.696 --> 00:01:57.172
What are some other ones? Let me think...

00:01:57.289 --> 00:02:00.047
Oh everybody's favorite: recalculating.

00:02:00.335 --> 00:02:06.614
I had to&nbsp;say the word 'approximately' approximately 168 times in a row.

00:02:06.731 --> 00:02:09.640
There is a red light camera&nbsp;approaching.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.368
I like to keep people safe.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:18.405
When I'm asked to use the voice, I do, because&nbsp;it's fun.

00:02:20.336 --> 00:02:25.123
My voice is going to live on forever? Wow the power is going to go to my head.

00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:28.080
I&nbsp;mean that's mind-blowing. Really. Isn't it?

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.460
You have reached your destination.

